+ * A/B interleaving deterministically in one thread and requires the mixed tuple to be rejected.
+ *
+ * COST, and the bound that actually holds. The snapshot is O(managers + budget): membership is a
+ * pointer-keyed set, so it does not degrade quadratically as contexts strand — the state this
+ * diagnostic explains — and it short-circuits entirely on an empty condemned set. The handle
+ * walk is bounded on RAW SLOTS, not on classified hits, which is the only bound worth stating:
+ * each sgen handle table is an SgenArrayList whose `next_slot` is a persistent high-water mark
+ * that sgen_gchandle_free never lowers (freeing only NULLs a slot), so a table that once grew
+ * large and is now mostly holes stays just as long as it was at its peak. A budget that merely
+ * skipped classification work past N hits would still sweep every one of those slots, four
+ * times over, while every bucket read 0 — a pause hazard on a single browser thread, and
+ * exactly what an earlier revision of this code did. ALC_CONDEMNED_HANDLE_SLOT_BUDGET is
+ * instead spent across the four passes as a cap on slot LOADS, and kinds 21/22 publish what the
+ * walk actually visited versus what it was eligible to visit, so the bound is observable rather
+ * than merely asserted. Truncation sets kind 18 and makes every count a lower bound.
+ *
+ * PURITY. Reading never mutates runtime state: the snapshot is built from the global ALC list
+ * plus each context's own manager arrays, the handle walk writes no slot at all (its callback
+ * returns nothing), and m_class_get_mem_manager is a pure lookup that cannot lazily allocate a
+ * manager (see the PRECONDITION note at sgen_scan_handles_into_managers). Gated exactly like
+ * the rest of the feature: this whole region is DISABLE_THREADS-only, the handle walk
+ * additionally requires sgen, and unavailable kinds keep returning -1.
+ */
+
+#define ALC_CONDEMNED_HANDLE_BUCKETS 4
+#if defined(HAVE_SGEN_GC) && (MONO_SGEN_CONDEMNED_HANDLE_BUCKETS != ALC_CONDEMNED_HANDLE_BUCKETS)
+#error "condemned handle bucket count must match the sgen scan contract in gc-internals.h"
+#endif
+
+/*
+ * RAW-SLOT budget for the handle walk, spent across all four type passes (see the COST note
+ * above for why the bound has to be on raw slots and not on classified hits). 200k slot loads is
+ * one to two orders of magnitude above the whole-process handle high-water mark this runtime has
+ * ever been measured at, so a healthy read is never truncated; the cap exists so a table with a
+ * pathological history can never turn a read-only gauge into a long pause on the single browser
+ * thread. Exceeding it sets kind 18 and makes kinds 11-14/19 lower bounds rather than silently
+ * understating them.
+ */
+#define ALC_CONDEMNED_HANDLE_SLOT_BUDGET 200000
+
+/*
+ * SELF-TEST budget behind kind 23. Reaching the real budget from a test would mean allocating
+ * 200k handles, which is neither cheap nor kind to a browser; kind 23 retakes the snapshot with
+ * this deliberately tiny cap instead, so the truncation path — kind 18 set, kinds 11-14/19 as
+ * lower bounds, kind 21 stopping short of kind 22 — is exercised on a table a test can build in
+ * a few hundred allocations. Deliberately not derived from the real budget: the regressions
+ * compare kind 21 against this exact number, and a computed value would let a mutant that
+ * widens the cap satisfy both sides.
+ */
+#define ALC_CONDEMNED_HANDLE_SELFTEST_SLOT_BUDGET 128
